---
title: Extensions
description: Find installable extensions, payment adapters, and registrar modules for FOSSBilling.
---

## Extension Directory

Browse the [Extension Directory](https://extensions.fossbilling.org/) for payment gateways, registrars, and other extensions that you can install from FOSSBilling.

Directory responses are cached for an hour. If a refresh fails, FOSSBilling uses the last valid response for up to 48 hours after it was fetched. Invalid responses do not replace the cached copy.

## Payment Adapters

The bundled Stripe and PayPal adapters both support one-time payments and subscriptions. For offline payments, see [Custom Payment Gateway](/admin-guide/custom-payment-gateway/).

[LiqPay](https://github.com/getnamingo/fossbilling-liqpay-gateway) and [Nicky.me](https://github.com/getnamingo/fossbilling-nicky-gateway) publish manual installation instructions. Check the adapter's compatibility and test it in staging before using it in production.

See [this GitHub issue](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/issues/1360) for broader discussion about payment adapter plans.

Building your own adapter? Start with [Creating a Payment Gateway](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-payment-gateway/).

## Registrar Modules

See [Supported Registrars](/admin-guide/product-types/domains/#supported-registrars) for bundled adapters and manual installation options.

Building your own registrar integration? See [Creating a Registrar Integration](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-registrar-integration/).

## Custom Extensions

For custom business logic, start with [Creating a Module](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-module/).

## How Do I Get My Extension Listed in the Extension Directory?

Open a pull request against the [extension-directory repository](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/extension-directory).
If you have questions, ask the team in the community channels before submitting.
